  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 53. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 史跡 — 昔の人の暮らしや出来事を伝える場所の跡。\n2. 下書き — 仕上げる前に試しに書く文章や絵。\n3. 親しみ — 身近に感じて心が引かれる気持ち。\n4. 下町 — 昔から商店や住宅などが集まる町の一帯。\n5. 試着 — 体に合うかなどを確かめるため衣服を着てみること。\n6. シチュー — 肉や野菜などを汁にとろみをつけて煮た料理。\n7. 市長 — 市の行政をまとめる長。\n8. 漆器 — 漆を塗って仕上げた器。\n9. 湿気 — 空気などに含まれる水分。\n10. 湿地 — 水分が多く湿っている土地。\n11. 執筆 — 文章を書くこと。\n12. 室内 — 部屋の中。\n13. 私鉄 — 国などの公共組織以外の会社が運営する鉄道。\n14. 市内 — ある市の区域の中。\n15. 品切れ — 売る品物の在庫がなくなること。\n16. シナリオ — 映画や劇などで使うせりふや場面を書いた台本。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
